# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The image only needs backend/, webapp/source, go.mod, go.sum and the
# migrations. Everything below is either dead weight or actively harmful.
#
# Why this file matters beyond build speed:
#
#   * webapp/node_modules — the Dockerfile runs `npm install` and THEN does
#     `COPY webapp/ ./`. Without this exclusion the host's node_modules is
#     copied over the container's freshly installed one, replacing the
#     `--ignore-scripts` install (which has no compiled esbuild binary) with
#     whatever the host happened to have. It tends to work on an x64 Linux
#     host purely by coincidence and breaks on anything else. This is the
#     single most important line in the file.
#
#   * firmware/esp32_s3_photoframe/secrets.h — contains the WiFi password and
#     the device token. It is not COPYed by the Dockerfile, but excluding it
#     guarantees it can never reach the daemon, an image layer, or a build
#     cache entry. Treat this as a hard requirement, not a nicety.
#
#   * data/ — the live SQLite database. It arrives via a bind mount at
#     runtime and must never be baked into an image.

# VCS and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github
.githooks

# Dependencies and build output
webapp/node_modules
webapp/dist
bin
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Runtime state — bind-mounted, never baked in
data/

# ESP32 firmware: not part of the server image, and it holds the secrets
firmware/

# Agent/tooling notes and editor config
.agent
.vscode
.devcontainer

# Local build/compose overrides
docker-compose.override.yml
